From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tyn <tyn@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:03:51 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] tyn: sg-pc title screen from the original Game.exe
 (TitleMenuType.SGHD)

The STEINS;GATE (Steam) title screen as the original draws and handles it, instead of the Chaos;Child title class with
estimated positions (a list on the left; the original has it on the right). Layout, art, timings and behaviour come
from the original Game.exe: the title draw dispatch on SW_TITLEMODE (0x4414f0), the main list (0x4411e0), the sub
lists (0x440600, 0x440be0, 0x441080), the decoration (0x4407f0), press start (0x4422e0), the button guide (0x436030),
the input routine (0x441650) and the hit areas at 0x52bf20.

- New generic class UI::SGHD::TitleMenu + Profile::SGHD::TitleMenu (TitleMenuType.SGHD): main entries, sub lists
  (with optional flag conditions), decoration, guide, positions and timings are profile data.
- Drawing per SW_TITLEMODE as the original: 0 fade in from black, 1 press start blinking over 64 frames, 2 fast blink,
  3 menu fading in with SW_TITLEDISPCT * 8 while the entries come in from 192 px to the right, 4 background and menu
  fading in, 5 as 3 under a screen opened from the title; blueprint pieces drawn every other frame, three of them
  shown at random and a bar of random length.
- Input as the original: up / down wrap (from "no entry" to the first), mouse / touch hover picks the entry (none in
  mouse mode until one is under the pointer), LOAD and EXTRA open a sub list in 32 frames (EXTRA has five entries
  once flag 860 is set, else CLEAR LIST and TIPS); while it is open only its entries take input and Back closes it;
  a chosen entry blinks for 64 frames, then SW_TITLECUR1 and SF_TITLEEND are set. The script waits in
  TitleMenu(Main) while a sub list is open or an entry blinks, so it does not act on those presses.
- sg-pc: hud/titlemenu.lua rewritten for the new class (no longer uses the CC title class).
- The satellite on the original title is a Bink 2 movie, which this engine does not play.

Checked on MuMu (Android 15): the title matches screenshots of the original (main list, LOAD and EXTRA sub lists,
key navigation step by step, guide); taps open the sub lists, Back closes them, LOAD opens the load screen and
returns to the title, CONFIG and HELP open; mo6tw-pc-zhs title unchanged.

